{"capturado_en": "2026-11-12T01:16:29+00:00", "respuesta": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Polylithic", "steam_appid": 1839060, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/be8861006841ef3c4e0b878a97a0ee4b.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=80 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's the Stone Age. Humans are not yet apex predators. We are, in fact, quite far down the list. You are a tribe leader. Your job is to take your people from desperate Paleolithic hunter-gatherers to the first permanent settlements of the Neolithic age, laying the foundations for all of human civilization. No pressure. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Along the way, you'll craft the earliest tools in human history, research technologies that separated us from every other species on Earth, build villages, manage a tribe, and navigate a world that is genuinely trying to eat you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Low-Poly World of Opportunity</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Polylithic world is vibrant, colorful, and almost entirely indifferent to your survival. Forage for resources across tall forests, snow-dusted hills, and rapids that do not care about your life. Hunt everything from rabbits to mammoths, each one a unique challenge, and each one a reminder that this is, technically, their world too. Seek out other human tribes, or what's left of them, learn from their mistakes, and then don’t do that.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Prehistoric Survival</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gather, craft, hunt, cook, and occasionally yell at wildlife; survival in the Stone Age is a full-time occupation. Master an evolving tech tree, experiment with a cooking system that generates recipes with predictably unpredictable results, and keep your body fed, rested, and functional. You can also tame a dog. Or a hyena. Both are loyal. One is slightly more alarming. Either way, companions eat, heal, follow commands, and will absolutely judge your decision-making</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Lay the Foundations of Civilization</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survival alone is one option. The other, the one that actually worked, is forming a tribe. As village leader, you'll manage your tribespeople's needs, grow your settlement, and guide them toward the Neolithic Revolution. They'll work, become Elders, and slowly, improbably, build something that resembles a civilization.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not everyone will welcome your progress. Enemy tribes have their own ideas about how prehistory should go. Sandbox Mode offers an infinitely generated world for those who prefer to skip the story and cause problems at their own pace. Customize your character (it's the Stone Age, somehow), emote around the campfire, and do your best to make prehistory turn into history.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Survive Together</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bring up to 9 friends into your Stone Age and form your own tribe. Share resources, coordinate hunts, build together, or completely ignore the plan and do your own thing; multiplayer makes every survival story unique, unpredictable, and significantly easier to blame on someone else.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/be8861006841ef3c4e0b878a97a0ee4b.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=80 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's the Stone Age. Humans are not yet apex predators. We are, in fact, quite far down the list. You are a tribe leader. Your job is to take your people from desperate Paleolithic hunter-gatherers to the first permanent settlements of the Neolithic age, laying the foundations for all of human civilization. No pressure. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Along the way, you'll craft the earliest tools in human history, research technologies that separated us from every other species on Earth, build villages, manage a tribe, and navigate a world that is genuinely trying to eat you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Low-Poly World of Opportunity</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/713b40d2b20200173701a5af4df1110d.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Polylithic world is vibrant, colorful, and almost entirely indifferent to your survival. Forage for resources across tall forests, snow-dusted hills, and rapids that do not care about your life. Hunt everything from rabbits to mammoths, each one a unique challenge, and each one a reminder that this is, technically, their world too. Seek out other human tribes, or what's left of them, learn from their mistakes, and then don’t do that.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Prehistoric Survival</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/6bf6c32f8c9c3a051cf454f7d1ba6c09.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gather, craft, hunt, cook, and occasionally yell at wildlife; survival in the Stone Age is a full-time occupation. Master an evolving tech tree, experiment with a cooking system that generates recipes with predictably unpredictable results, and keep your body fed, rested, and functional. You can also tame a dog. Or a hyena. Both are loyal. One is slightly more alarming. Either way, companions eat, heal, follow commands, and will absolutely judge your decision-making</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Lay the Foundations of Civilization</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.poster.avif?t=1793823381\" width=780 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.webm?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/extras/efefa63745b3ab14a605239b80a371aa.mp4?t=1793823381\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survival alone is one option. The other, the one that actually worked, is forming a tribe. As village leader, you'll manage your tribespeople's needs, grow your settlement, and guide them toward the Neolithic Revolution. They'll work, become Elders, and slowly, improbably, build something that resembles a civilization.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not everyone will welcome your progress. Enemy tribes have their own ideas about how prehistory should go. Sandbox Mode offers an infinitely generated world for those who prefer to skip the story and cause problems at their own pace. Customize your character (it's the Stone Age, somehow), emote around the campfire, and do your best to make prehistory turn into history.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Survive Together</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bring up to 9 friends into your Stone Age and form your own tribe. Share resources, coordinate hunts, build together, or completely ignore the plan and do your own thing; multiplayer makes every survival story unique, unpredictable, and significantly easier to blame on someone else.</p>", "short_description": "Polylithic is a survival game unlike any other, set in the most pivotal moment in mankind's history. Experience life as a Paleolithic hunter-gatherer, settle down as a Neolithic farmer, form tribes in co-op multiplayer, or go it alone in a world where the apex predator is still a distant aspiration.", "supported_languages": "English, Czech, French, German, Russian, Japanese, Spanish - Spain, Portuguese - Brazil, Simplified Chinese, Italian, Korean", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/1df7c44279065a14e15874b670f16a8fc9f4a481/header.jpg?t=1793823381", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/99564d61f6ae61853a054d1064349bb43279cc8d/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793823381", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1839060/99564d61f6ae61853a054d1064349bb43279cc8d/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793823381", "website": "https://www.polyperfect.com/polylithic", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating sy